From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 18:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: prefer four-lane DP on Orange Pi 5B

The Type-C monitor advertises both the four-lane DisplayPort-only pin
assignments C/E and the two-lane multi-function assignment D.  Advertising
all capabilities from the Orange Pi side lets the sink's multi-function
preference select D, limiting the link to two HBR3 lanes and forcing the
3840x2160p60 stream down to RGB888.

Describe the source capabilities explicitly and omit assignment D.  This
causes DisplayPort Alt Mode to select assignment C (or E where appropriate),
making all four SuperSpeed pairs available to DisplayPort.  USB 2.0 remains
available, but USB 3.x is intentionally unavailable while DP Alt Mode is
active.

The VDO describes a receptacle acting as DFP_D, HBR3 signalling, and pin
assignments C/E.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dtsi
@@ -324,7 +324,7 @@
 			altmodes {
 				displayport {
 					svid = /bits/ 16 <0xff01>;
-					vdo = <0xffffffff>;
+					vdo = <0x00001446>;
 				};
 			};
 
